n for middle-aged and older Italian men to carry extra weight around their midsection. If your cousin is interacting heavily with older demographics, this could skew their perception. **5. Fashion and clothing fit** Italian men are famous for their tailoring and fashion, which heavily favors slim, form-fitting clothing. In countries like the US, men often wear looser, baggier clothing that hides body shape. In Italy, a fitted shirt or tailored suit will make any extra weight—or a broad, muscular chest—much more visible. So, while Italian men are statistically leaner than men in many other Western countries, regional location, age, fashion, and your cousin's own frame of reference could easily explain why they seem to have a heavier build!
